    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **273 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented owner registration dates so that when an owner is created without one, it defaults to today's date, and is returned in the owner response as `registrationDate` in ISO format (`YYYY-MM-DD`).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string`, `format: date`, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema. The OpenAPI generator maps this to a `LocalDate` on `OwnerDto`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java` entity** \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to the `registration_date` column, with getter/setter, and a `@PrePersist` hook (`onRegister()`) that defaults it to `LocalDate.now()` when null. This fires on both the `jpa` and `spring-data-jpa` persistence paths (both use `em.persist` for new entities).\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres); hsqldb is the one exercised by the tests.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` picks up the field automatically by matching name/type, so no mapper change was needed. The new `Cp08Tests` acceptance test (`registrationDate` defaults to today) passes, along with the existing 27 owner controller tests and the entire suite.",
